
# type(scope): imperative summary, lower-case, no full stop (72 chars max)
#   types:  feat fix perf refactor revert test docs build ci chore style
#   scopes: frontend passkey-sdk factory relayer perch infra docs deps
#   (.github/pr-checks.json is the list; scope is optional)
#
# The same structure as the PR description, in miniature. Wrap at 72.
# feat/fix/perf/refactor/revert commits need the Why paragraph.
#
# Why: the problem with the current code, and why this approach rather
# than the obvious alternative. Numbers for any cost or size claim.
#
# What changes: what a user, dApp or integrator sees differently, and
# what deliberately does not change.
#
# Evidence: `cargo test -p nido-integration-tests --test it` 88 passed;
# what was not run, and why.
#
# Trailers, one per line, after a blank line:
# Refs: #123
# Security: F2, W3      (docs/SECURITY_INVARIANTS.md IDs, or "none")
# BREAKING-CHANGE: what breaks and how to migrate (with "!" in the subject)
#
# Not here: review logs, agent prompts, "addressed review comments".
# Use it: git config commit.template .gitmessage
